-- Update untouched defaults only; preserve owner-written briefs and all saved ideas.
UPDATE design_entries SET content=json_set(content,'$.text','Develop The garden kitchen across the confirmed A+B+C volume. A is the long WEST glass extension with an eight-seat oak dining table running NORTH–SOUTH. B is the shallow NORTH return, now a casual breakfast area with two stools on the NORTH side of a low L counter; remove the sofa. C keeps the original kitchen and D keeps the cooker on its EAST wall. Narrow and shift the NORTH–SOUTH oak island west to widen the cooking aisle, targeting 1.3–1.4 m subject to a survey. Place two island stools with knee room at its SOUTH short end, outside the working aisle. Add a low EAST–WEST return at the north end of C, joining the east cabinetry, with a second oven underneath opening SOUTH into the kitchen and extra drawers. Add tall pantry storage at the northeast of C. Keep the original range oven. The low return separates breakfast seating without a full-height wall blocking north light. Preserve dining space and clear routes around chairs, stools and open oven doors. Use honed creamy natural stone with substantial organic taupe veining and mineral variation, pale oak, muted sage cabinetry and slim dark glazing. The table and island stay parallel: from the west garden the table is nearest, the island behind, and the east cooker farthest away. Use kitchen-garden-breakfast-v4-plan.svg, its fixed model and kitchen-camera-orientation-v4.svg; never rotate or mirror the plan. The confirmed A+B outline is unchanged. Open old west and north boundaries around retained piers as a structural proposal. Roof form, heights, heated integration and the actual stamped approval remain to be verified. Earlier layouts are archived. AI views convey atmosphere, not measured geometry.'),version=version+1,updated_at=strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%fZ','now') WHERE project='kitchen' AND kind='brief' AND json_extract(content,'$.text')='Develop the selected Social kitchen across the full confirmed A+B+C volume. A is the long WEST extension with an eight-seat dining table running north–south. B is the shallow NORTH return with one sofa and a coffee table. C is the enlarged original kitchen with a generous freestanding oak island running north–south; D, the cooker, stays on its EAST wall. Open the former west and north boundaries around retained piers as a structural proposal. Keep the confirmed outline and proportions: do not rotate, mirror, deepen B or enlarge the envelope. Use the Social kitchen plan and fixed spatial model to control geometry. Explore pale oak, limestone, sage range cabinetry, slim dark glazing and a low insulated extension roof with oak soffits; retain the original white kitchen ceiling. Use the original interior and garden photographs for views and distinguish photo-based views from inferred new viewpoints. AI images convey atmosphere and finishes; they do not establish dimensions, roof or structure. The alternative layouts remain in the archive. Furniture fit, openings, ceiling heights, services and the actual approved drawings remain to be verified.';
UPDATE design_entries SET content=json_set(content,'$.text','Develop Lounge by the fire with Gather under the eaves as one selected courtyard arrangement. Keep the fireside lounge in the west wing and a long outdoor timber dining table in the perpendicular north bay, with a low natural-stone-topped serving and storage counter against the timber wall. Create cozy seating around the existing fireplace with natural wood, oatmeal cushions and warm restrained lighting. Preserve the existing roof, posts, enclosing house, tree, lawn, door access and pool connection. Keep the dining table parallel to its wall counter. Refine this configuration from the reference photographs; do not exchange the lounge and dining bays. Other courtyard layouts, including the daybed variations, remain in the clickable archive. Renders are spatial interpretations; verify furniture sizes, chair pull-out space, rain coverage, fireplace safety clearances and routes against a measured plan.'),version=version+1,updated_at=strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%fZ','now') WHERE project='courtyard' AND kind='brief' AND json_extract(content,'$.text')='Explore the whole courtyard behind the pool with an eating area, a lounge with two daybeds and cozy seats in every layout. Keep the existing L-shaped arrangement, including the long slightly angled west wing, the shallow north loggia, and its uncovered front terrace. Retain the roof, posts, existing outdoor fireplace, timber character, tree and pool. Compare three source-based isometric studies: A, a generous banquette table at the north terrace with west-wing daybeds and fireside chairs; B, two north-bay daybeds with a round outdoor dining table in front and cozy fireside chairs; C, a compact dining nook and separate sofa in the north bay, plus west-wing daybeds and fireside chairs. Use natural timber furniture, soft oatmeal and sage fabrics and restrained stone details. Keep routes to the house, adjoining rooms and pool practical. The isometric illustrations omit the existing roof only to reveal the arrangement; this is not a roof-removal or pergola proposal. The source-plan outline governs the layout. Furniture, tree position, glazed opening details and heights remain indicative; verify door swings, chair pull-out space, rain coverage and fit with a survey. Earlier concepts remain available in the archive.';
